  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 6.3.2, 'OpenHIE architectural diagram illustrating mechanisms for interoperability across different applications'. Within a DIGITAL HEALTH PLATFORM, the OpenHIE component layer holds business domain services — (1) logistics management information system, (2) shared health record and (3) health management information system — and registry services — (4) terminology services, (5) client registry, (6) facility registry, (7) health worker registry and (8) product registry. Beneath them, (9) the interoperability services layer provides authentication, an interlinking service and entity mapping. Below the platform sit (10) point-of-service applications: mobile system, electronic medical record, health management information system, lab, pharmacy and logistics management information system. A legend defines each numbered component — for example, that the interoperability layer receives all communications from external services and orchestrates data exchange with the component layer. Adapted from OpenHIE architecture v2, 2019.",
